          "literatureReview": "Weil Felix test detects cross-reacting antibodies to Proteus vulgaris OX antigens. Normal: <1:80 titer. Significant: ≥1:160 titer. OX-2: epidemic typhus, OX-19: murine typhus/scrub typhus, OX-K: spotted fever group. Becomes positive 7-10 days after infection. Low sensitivity and specificity. False positives with other infections. Confirm with immunofluorescence or PCR. Used in resource-limited settings for rickettsial disease diagnosis. Critical for typhus fever diagnosis in endemic areas."
